    emmo:elucidation "A representation of current as a sinusoidal integral quantity using a complex quantity whose argument is equal to the initial phase and whose modulus is equal to the root-mean-square value."@en ;
    emmo:note "A phasor is a constant complex number, usually expressed in exponential form, representing the complex amplitude (magnitude and phase) of a sinusoidal function of time. Phasors are used by electrical engineers to simplify computations involving sinusoids, where they can often reduce a differential equation problem to an algebraic one."@en ;
    emmo:qudtReference "https://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectricCurrentPhasor"^^xsd:string ;
    emmo:wikidataReference "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q78514596"^^xsd:string .

