        emmo:EMMO_868ae137_4d25_493e_b270_21ea3d94849e,
        emmo:EMMO_ab79e92b_5377_454d_be06_d61b50db295a,
        emmo:EMMO_b081b346_7279_46ef_9a3d_2c088fcd79f4 ;
    rdfs:label "Statcoulomb"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The statcoulomb (statC) or franklin (Fr) or electrostatic unit of charge (esu) is the physical unit for electrical charge used in the centimetre-gram-second system of units (cgs) and Gaussian units. It is a derived unit given by 1 statC = 1 g cm s = 1 erg cm. The SI system of units uses the coulomb (C) instead. The conversion between C and statC is different in different contexts. The number 2997924580 is 10 times the value of the speed of light expressed in meters/second, and the conversions are exact except where indicated. The coulomb is an extremely large charge rarely encountered in electrostatics, while the statcoulomb is closer to everyday charges.

-- QUDT"""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/unclassifiedunits-abox#>,
        "http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel "Statcoulomb"@en ;
    emmo:EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf 3.335641e-10 ;
    emmo:EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd 0e+00 ;
    emmo:elucidation """The statcoulomb (statC) or franklin (Fr) or electrostatic unit of charge (esu) is the physical unit for electrical charge used in the centimetre-gram-second system of units (cgs) and Gaussian units. It is a derived unit given by 1 statC = 1 g cm s = 1 erg cm. The SI system of units uses the coulomb (C) instead. The conversion between C and statC is different in different contexts. The number 2997924580 is 10 times the value of the speed of light expressed in meters/second, and the conversions are exact except where indicated. The coulomb is an extremely large charge rarely encountered in electrostatics, while the statcoulomb is closer to everyday charges.

-- QUDT"""@en ;
    emmo:qudtReference "http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/C_Stat"^^xsd:string ;
    emmo:unitSymbol "statC"^^xsd:string ;
    emmo:wikipediaReference "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statcoulomb?oldid=492664360"^^xsd:string .

emmo:StatcoulombPerMole a owl:NamedIndividual,
        emmo:EMMO_8246541a_f1f6_4d03_8bd7_fc6b76d17375,
        emmo:EMMO_868ae137_4d25_493e_b270_21ea3d94849e,
        emmo:EMMO_b081b346_7279_46ef_9a3d_2c088fcd79f4,
        emmo:EMMO_e6110006_88b9_45cd_9f9c_a2a91c0c21f8 ;
    rdfs:label "StatcoulombPerMole"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """"Statcoulomb per Mole" is a unit of measure for the electical charge associated with one mole of a substance. The mole is a unit of measurement used in chemistry to express amounts of a chemical substance, defined as an amount of a substance that contains as many elementary entities (e.g., atoms, molecules, ions, electrons) as there are atoms in 12 grams of pure carbon-12 (12C), the isotope of carbon with atomic weight 12.

-- QUDT"""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/unclassifiedunits-abox#>,
        "http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:altLabel "Statcoulomb per Mole"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "StatcoulombPerMole"@en ;
    emmo:EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf 3.33564e-10 ;
    emmo:EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd 0e+00 ;
    emmo:elucidation """"Statcoulomb per Mole" is a unit of measure for the electical charge associated with one mole of a substance. The mole is a unit of measurement used in chemistry to express amounts of a chemical substance, defined as an amount of a substance that contains as many elementary entities (e.g., atoms, molecules, ions, electrons) as there are atoms in 12 grams of pure carbon-12 (12C), the isotope of carbon with atomic weight 12.

-- QUDT"""@en ;
    emmo:qudtReference "http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/C_Stat-PER-MOL"^^xsd:string ;
    emmo:unitSymbol "statC/mol"^^xsd:string .

emmo:StatcoulombPerSquareCentiMetre a owl:NamedIndividual,
