    emmo:EMMO_d4e0a0ab_2f67_4f87_a0db_b544e6dceed4 emmo:Byte ;
    emmo:elucidation """The terabyte is a multiple of the unit byte for digital information. The prefix tera means 10¹² in the International System of Units (SI), and therefore 1 terabyte is 1000000000000bytes, or 1 trillion bytes, or 1000 gigabytes. 1 terabyte in binary prefixes is 0.9095 tebibytes, or 931.32 gibibytes. The unit symbol for the terabyte is TB or TByte, but not Tb (lower case b) which refers to terabit.

-- QUDT"""@en ;
