    skos:prefLabel "SourceCode"@en ;
    emmo:elucidation "A programming language entity expressing a formal detailed plan of what a software is intended to do."@en ;
    emmo:note "A source code is the companion of an application, being it the entity used to generate the application list of CPU executable instructions."@en,
        "Source code (also referred to as source or code) is the version of software as it is originally written (i.e., typed into a computer) by a human in plain text (i.e., human readable alphanumeric characters)."@en .

