emmo:EMMO_bc37743c_37c4_4ec7_9d58_d1aae5567352 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Substance"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A matter entity characterised by the fact that it possesses some homogeneous properties or identification criteria."@en,
        """A substance is an aggregate of particulate matter that shows an homogeneity of property, according to some criteria. A substance is an intermediate concept between generic matter and more specific categorizations. A substance can be either continuum or mesoscopic.
The word substance here refers to a concept that is unrelated with aristotelic philosophy."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/reference/physicalistic#> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf emmo:EMMO_41cecfc2_bb6b_45f3_b6cc_e7740d931afe,
        emmo:EMMO_57d977ab_0036_4779_b59a_e47620afdb9c ;
    skos:example "A litre of water."@en,
        "A pen can be classified as a substance (although it has parts with different properties) since it can be identified as being solid."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Substance"@en ;
    emmo:OWLRL2DLAxioms "Disjoint Union Of: MesoscopicSubstance, ContinuumSubstance"^^xsd:string ;
    emmo:conceptualisation """A substance is an aggregate of particulate matter that shows an homogeneity of property, according to some criteria. A substance is an intermediate concept between generic matter and more specific categorizations. A substance can be either continuum or mesoscopic.
The word substance here refers to a concept that is unrelated with aristotelic philosophy."""@en ;
    emmo:elucidation "A matter entity characterised by the fact that it possesses some homogeneous properties or identification criteria."@en ;
    emmo:note "A substance is always 4D self-connected, meaning that it represents only entities within a time interval that ensure self-connectivity. For example, the entity made of a bag of powder that is parceled up into portions and used in different applications is a single substance."@en .

emmo:EMMO_c130614a_2985_476d_a7ed_8a137847703c a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "IntentionalAgent"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "An agent that is driven by the intention to reach a defined objective in driving a process."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/reference/workflow#> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/agency> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty [ owl:inverseOf emmo:EMMO_cd24eb82_a11c_4a31_96ea_32f870c5580a ] ;
            owl:someValuesFrom emmo:EMMO_bafc17b5_9be4_4823_8bbe_ab4e90b6738c ],
        emmo:EMMO_2480b72b_db8d_460f_9a5f_c2912f979046 ;
    skos:prefLabel "IntentionalAgent"@en ;
    emmo:elucidation "An agent that is driven by the intention to reach a defined objective in driving a process."@en ;
    emmo:note "Intentionality is not limited to human agents, but in general to all agents that have the capacity to decide to act in driving a process according to a motivation."@en .

